WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:09.100
It may sound strange, but as liberal, I do
believe in American exceptionalism.

00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:14.070
Due to our democratic ideals and personal
freedoms, America is a unique and special

00:00:14.070 --> 00:00:16.500
country in the world.

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:21.130
You may remember back in 2009 when President
Obama said he didn't really believe in American

00:00:21.130 --> 00:00:26.710
Exceptionalism, saying "I believe in American
exceptionalism, just as I suspect that the

00:00:26.710 --> 00:00:31.860
Brits believe in British exceptionalism and
the Greeks believe in Greek exceptionalism."

00:00:31.860 --> 00:00:37.500
In and of itself there's nothing wrong with
Obama's general idea here in which each individual

00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:42.250
country is filled with proud people who believe
their country is unique and special in the

00:00:42.250 --> 00:00:43.250
world.

00:00:43.250 --> 00:00:48.590
Actually, if this idea fuels people to build
a better society they can be genuinely proud

00:00:48.590 --> 00:00:50.159
of, then fantastic.

00:00:50.159 --> 00:00:55.600
Of course by the same token, this nationalism
could also push otherwise good people to believe

00:00:55.600 --> 00:01:00.690
they should have a sway over the world or
influence other nations because they are morally

00:01:00.690 --> 00:01:02.340
superior.

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:07.520
Over the eight years of Obama's presidency,
he walked back his statement, and did actually

00:01:07.520 --> 00:01:10.940
say that America's exceptionalism was unique.

00:01:10.940 --> 00:01:15.560
For me, there is an additional reason for
American exceptionalism which goes beyond

00:01:15.560 --> 00:01:19.190
just our democratic ideals and personal freedoms.

00:01:19.190 --> 00:01:23.030
Of course we aren't the only country in the
world to share in those ideas.

00:01:23.030 --> 00:01:28.080
It is also the additional piece America is
a country of immigrants, a country of people

00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:32.970
from all of the world who came here to make
a better live for themselves.

00:01:32.970 --> 00:01:38.159
We are a nation built by people whose ancestors
often came here with nothing, and who worked

00:01:38.159 --> 00:01:43.340
hard to build a better country and life for
their children and their children's children.

00:01:43.340 --> 00:01:47.230
While we certainly aren't the only country
to welcome immigrants or build a solid middle

00:01:47.230 --> 00:01:52.470
class, there is no other nation on Earth that
more people from more countries have come

00:01:52.470 --> 00:01:57.130
to live and prosper because of the pursuit
of happiness.

00:01:57.130 --> 00:02:00.920
This doesn't mean everyone can come here and
we can have open borders, but it does mean

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:05.890
that if you come here legally, you will be
given the same chance a natural born citizen

00:02:05.890 --> 00:02:06.890
has.

00:02:06.890 --> 00:02:11.640
Even today, as we live in a politically fractured
society and many will tell you things have

00:02:11.640 --> 00:02:15.410
never been worse, the the truth is things
have actually never been better.

00:02:15.410 --> 00:02:22.040
Now of course I don't mean that for every
specific person or every specific job or industry.

00:02:22.040 --> 00:02:24.580
Times change and so do people and economies.

00:02:24.580 --> 00:02:29.780
But as a whole, America has done an incredible
job of welcoming so many diverse people, having

00:02:29.780 --> 00:02:35.040
us all share in the American dream while at
the same time all being able to keep traditions

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:38.090
and practices from our unique cultures.

00:02:38.090 --> 00:02:43.670
As our economy changes over the next few years,
we the people have a massive job of changing

00:02:43.670 --> 00:02:44.670
along with it.

00:02:44.670 --> 00:02:50.630
In an age where supermarkets will be automated
and driverless cars will replace truck drivers,

00:02:50.630 --> 00:02:55.360
it will be more important than ever for us
to change with technology.

00:02:55.360 --> 00:03:00.020
The world doesn't stop for anyone or owe you
anything, you have to adapt to a changing

00:03:00.020 --> 00:03:01.020
world.

00:03:01.020 --> 00:03:06.050
And in these moments of change is when America
has been at its best.

00:03:06.050 --> 00:03:12.500
Our system, built on the idea that it's your
job to pursue your happiness is the reason

00:03:12.500 --> 00:03:17.700
that more people still want to come to America
right now than any other country on Earth.

00:03:17.700 --> 00:03:22.140
I always find it ironic that so many people
who rant and rave about how evil America is

00:03:22.140 --> 00:03:25.470
are the same people who demand we let anyone
in here.

00:03:25.470 --> 00:03:31.260
Why would anyone want to come to such an evil,
unfair and oppressive society?

00:03:31.260 --> 00:03:33.860
Of course this is nonsense and they know it.

00:03:33.860 --> 00:03:38.200
There's a reason that people don't leave America
in droves, even the celebrities who said they

00:03:38.200 --> 00:03:41.430
would leave if Trump was elected have some
how managed to stay here.

00:03:41.430 --> 00:03:45.900
For the record, I'm pretty sure Canada is
happy it didn't have to take in most of them

00:03:45.900 --> 00:03:46.900
anyway.

00:03:46.900 --> 00:03:50.790
I mention all this because for all the goodness
here in America, we obviously still have some

00:03:50.790 --> 00:03:51.800
work to do.

00:03:51.800 --> 00:03:57.140
Every society has work to do, which is why
the people peddling utopia are frauds and

00:03:57.140 --> 00:03:58.140
liars.

00:03:58.140 --> 00:04:03.080
In America though, almost every generation
has fought to expand rights to other people,

00:04:03.080 --> 00:04:04.500
not to limit them.

00:04:04.500 --> 00:04:09.110
That's how women got the right to vote, that's
how we freed the slaves, that's how gay people

00:04:09.110 --> 00:04:14.730
were allowed to marry and that's how whatever
will come next will arrive.

00:04:14.730 --> 00:04:19.530
As for that work we have to do, I think a
lot of it has to be done on how we can come

00:04:19.530 --> 00:04:22.030
together, not rip each other apart.

00:04:22.030 --> 00:04:25.710
I'm a firm believer that most of us want the
same things in life.

00:04:25.710 --> 00:04:30.479
We want to work a decent job, eat some good
food, have some sex and go on vacation now

00:04:30.479 --> 00:04:31.710
and again.

00:04:31.710 --> 00:04:36.219
Most of us aren't racist homophobes secretly
plotting against each other and trying to

00:04:36.219 --> 00:04:38.990
push our way of life on everyone else.

00:04:38.990 --> 00:04:44.400
This is somewhere which no matter your political
leanings we can all come together.

00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:49.169
Yes, some of us are from big cities, some
of us are from small towns, some of us had

00:04:49.169 --> 00:04:53.580
ancestors who arrived on the mayflower and
some of us just arrived yesterday, but the

00:04:53.580 --> 00:05:01.379
only way this all works is if we all bend
to fit American ideals of freedom of liberty,

00:05:01.379 --> 00:05:04.610
not if we demand the system bend to us.

00:05:04.610 --> 00:05:06.800
My guest this week is comedian Trae Crowder.

00:05:06.800 --> 00:05:10.559
Trae is known as the liberal redneck...apparently
they do exist.

00:05:10.559 --> 00:05:15.509
His comedy is a blend of showing liberal elites
that rednecks aren't all backwards hicks and

00:05:15.509 --> 00:05:19.029
showing rednecks that liberals aren't all
evil socialists.

00:05:19.029 --> 00:05:21.409
It's almost as if we should judge people as
individuals, not as groups.

00:05:21.409 --> 00:05:24.180
I feel like I've heard that somewhere before.

00:05:24.180 --> 00:05:28.580
The middle of this country for a long time
has been the brunt of jokes and the easy way

00:05:28.580 --> 00:05:33.909
to make fun of anyone who thinks differently
than people in New York or LA.

00:05:33.909 --> 00:05:38.699
As someone who has only lived in New York
or LA, I've never subscribed to this way of

00:05:38.699 --> 00:05:43.289
thinking and have tried not to mock people
just because they talk differently or haven't

00:05:43.289 --> 00:05:47.160
evolved on some of their social views the
second that I have.

00:05:47.160 --> 00:05:51.409
Whether your Democrat or Republican, straight
or gay, black or white, native American or

00:05:51.409 --> 00:05:56.219
new immigrant, this country belongs to all
of us and it needs all of us to continue to

00:05:56.219 --> 00:05:57.900
make it better.

00:05:57.900 --> 00:06:01.080
That's the thing with exceptionalism, it take
an awful lot of work to keep up.

